# Project Work Log

## 2026-11-10 - Full Stack DPI ML System Integration & Interactive Developer UI

- **Summary**: Transformed the DPI Python repository into a production-grade, interactive full-stack network intelligence platform with FastAPI bridge and Next.js 16 developer dashboard.
- **Details (The 'What')**:
  - Cloned and analyzed the `Minor_Project-KGEC_25-27` codebase (packet capture, feature extraction, flow management, and decision tree inference).
  - Installed and verified global and workspace skills (`ui_ux_pro_max`, `frontend_design`, `enhance_ui`, `daily_log`, `web_performance_optimization`).
  - Resolved Python 3.14 dependencies (`joblib`, `scikit-learn`, `python-multipart`).
  - Fixed test runner import resolution in `tests/test_dpi.py` (all 13 unit tests passing).
  - Implemented `dpi/server.py` — an asynchronous FastAPI server supporting:
    - Real-time telemetry (`/api/status`, `/api/interfaces`)
    - Remote capture triggers (`/api/capture/start`, `/api/capture/stop`)
    - Offline PCAP upload & replay (`/api/capture/upload-pcap`) with thread-isolated asyncio event loop
    - Bidirectional flow inspection (`/api/flows`, `/api/flows/{key}`)
    - Packet inspection stream (`/api/packets`)
    - On-demand ML prediction (`/api/model/predict`) & feature importance ranking (`/api/model/importance`)
    - WebSocket telemetry streaming (`/ws/live`)
  - Built comprehensive Next.js 16 frontend in `apps/web`:
    - Responsive dark mode security theme conforming to `ui_ux_pro_max`
    - Top header with live capture status radar and packet counters
    - Tab navigation (`Overview`, `Capture & PCAP`, `Flow Explorer`, `Packet Inspector`, `ML Studio`)
    - Slide-over Feature Inspector with 25 statistical features and Decision Tree class probabilities
    - Interactive ML Diagnostic Studio with simulation presets
  - Conducted end-to-end browser inspection and verified UI rendering via automated browser agent.
- **Decisions (The 'Why')**:
  - Chose FastAPI with threadpool worker isolation for PyShark to prevent event loop blocking on Windows with Python 3.14.
  - Selected a Data-Dense + Drill-Down pattern recommended by `ui_ux_pro_max` to optimize for developer productivity and deep packet analysis.
  - Retained both polling fallback and WebSocket real-time updates to ensure reliable telemetry even if connections drop.
- **Blockers & Open Questions**:
  - `model/train.py` is currently empty in the original repository; a retraining pipeline can be added next if custom datasets are provided.
- **Next Steps**:
  - Add packet export to PCAP / CSV from the browser.
  - Implement custom BPF filter builder with validation.
